---
import { siteUrl } from "../../../lib/routes.mjs";
---

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="landing-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
            <h2 id="landing-title">
                <svg class="site-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <use
                        href={siteUrl("plant-icons.svg#icon-observation")}
                        width="64"
                        height="64"
                    ></use>
                </svg>
                Installed landing sequence
            </h2>
            <p>Actual move-in, shakedown, riser finish, and Monday baseline.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prep-strip">
        <article class="prep-day" data-date="2026-07-30">
            <div class="prep-date">
                <strong>Jul 30</strong>
                <span>Thursday</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Camera + reflector ready</h3>
            <p>
                The 256 GB card passed test recording. Full-height Mylar is on the divider, floor
                Mylar protects the carpet, and the light is rotated window-to-room.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-day move-day" data-date="2026-07-31">
            <div class="prep-date">
                <strong>Jul 31</strong>
                <span>Friday</span>
            </div>
            <h3>RO water + early move-in</h3>
            <p>
                Around 4 a.m., water only dry pots and drain. Arrange both tables, start the
                40%-at-20-inch shakedown, and record the first sensor reading after conditions
                stabilize.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-day" data-date="2026-08-01">
            <div class="prep-date">
                <strong>Aug 1</strong>
                <span>Saturday</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Risers + cable safety</h3>
            <p>
                After lights-off, install the height-first three-by-four map: +5.11 under A3/B1,
                +1.18 under B2/C2, +3.93 under D3/A2, and +2.75 under D2/C3. Keep A1, C1, D1, and B3
                direct. Then restore the 20-inch LED-to-tip clearance; align the round table at the
                window end and the wooden table toward the room; secure wall cables,
                <a href={siteUrl("setup/archive/layout/#wiring")}>add drip loops</a>, and finish the
                removable lower-window block.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="prep-day" data-date="2026-08-02">
            <div class="prep-date">
                <strong>Aug 2</strong>
                <span>Sunday</span>
            </div>
            <h3>Lock the baseline</h3>
            <p>
                Hold 40% at 20 inches. Review the GrowCam framing, tissue-test the fan, inspect the
                lit surfaces, photograph the final riser layout, and log the sensor baseline.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>
    <div class="priority-note">
        <strong>
            <svg class="site-icon" viewBox="0 0 64 64" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                <use href={siteUrl("plant-icons.svg#icon-caution")} width="64" height="64"></use>
            </svg>
            Important
        </strong>
        <p>
            Historical August 28 baseline: the AW200SE was 45% at 18 inches, two E6 Gen2/E25 fans
            provide opposing gentle sweeps, and P01–P18 are in pot setup 2: three parts Molly’s to
            two parts perlite by volume. That phase held those settings while measuring the first
            comparable dry-down. Seven days is a review target, not a recurring watering date. Keep
            setup-1 weights historical. Canonical History records the first setup-2 plain
            Beauchamp's RO soak at 4:22 p.m. on August 26 and Wet weights from 12:14–12:20 a.m. on
            August 27. Preserve that nearly eight-hour interval; these are not 30–60-minute drainage
            readings. Start the
            <a href="https://github.com/Nick2bad4u/Gardening/blob/main/docs/equipment/msu-fertilizer-schedule.md">
                dilute MSU sequence
            </a>
            only at the following ready watering.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
